  "body": "The `event.source` property on message events dispatched from `BroadcastChannel` instances seems to return `null` in browsers. I believe this should be explicitly mentioned in [BroadcastChannel.postMessage](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/web-messaging.html#dom-broadcastchannel-postmessage).\r\n\r\nThe `BroadcastChannel` API is a cross-document messaging mechanism, so the spec seems to imply that `event.source` should be a `WindowProxy` instead of `null` (found in [the MessageEvent interface](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/comms.html#the-messageevent-interface)):\r\n\r\n> The source attribute must return the value it was initialized to\\. It represents, in cross\\-document messaging, the WindowProxy of the browsing context of the Window object from which the message came; and in the connect events used by shared workers, the newly connecting MessagePort\\.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nRelated: [Event.source Returns null in BroadcastChannel](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/57937512/event-source-returns-null-in-broadcastchannel-javascript) on StackOverflow (no answers).\r\n\r\n",
